1. Prepare Python on Your Laptop
 * Open Command Prompt (cmd) and verify Python:
   python --version

 * If missing, download it from python.org/downloads and check "Add python.exe to PATH" before installing (or use your Anaconda Python path).
2. Install Dependencies
 * In Command Prompt, run:
   python -m pip install ultralytics supervision opencv-python fastapi uvicorn

3. Set Up Your Phone as a Webcam
 * Install DroidCam or Iriun Webcam on your phone and laptop.
 * Connect via USB cable and confirm the camera feed works.
4. Organize Project Files
 * Keep both files in the same folder:
   * Queue killer.py
   * customer_queue_view.html
5. Adjust Camera & Detection Zones
 * Open Queue killer.py.
 * Change CAMERA_INDEX to 1 or 2 if your phone camera isn't detected at 0.
 * Adjust QUEUE_ZONE_POINTS and SERVICE_ZONE_POINTS to fit your camera's physical queue and service areas.
6. Set Up ngrok & HTML
 * Download ngrok.exe from ngrok.com/download into your project folder.
 * Add your auth token:
   ngrok config add-authtoken YOUR_TOKEN

 * Start the tunnel in a terminal:
   ngrok http 8000

 * Open customer_queue_view.html, find const API_BASE, and set it to:
   const API_BASE = "https://sermon-sports-obstruct.ngrok-free.dev";

7. Run the Script
 * In your project folder, start the backend:
   python "Queue killer.py"

8. Customer Ticket Link
 * Users access their token directly at:
   https://sermon-sports-obstruct.ngrok-free.dev/new-ticket

 * Tap "Visit Site" if the ngrok free warning appears.
 * The link automatically issues the next ticket number and displays real-time wait times and queue positions.
